<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">

    <meta
        name="viewport"
        content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"
    >

    <meta
        name="description"
        content="Permanent lesson-creation standard for Elmi Guray Academy HTML and AI developer courses."
    >

    <title>
        EGA Permanent HTML Lesson Template
    </title>

<style id="ega-official-logo-style">
  .ega-official-logo {
    width: 190px;
    height: 190px;
    display: block;
    margin: 20px auto;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: center;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 5px solid #ffffff;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.18);
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .ega-official-logo {
      width: 150px;
      height: 150px;
    }
  }
</style>

</head>

<body>

    \1

        <img
            src="../ega-logo.png"
            alt="Elmi Guray Academy official logo"
            class="ega-official-logo"
        >

        <h1>
            Elmi Guray Academy
        </h1>

        <h2>
            Permanent HTML Lesson-Creation Standard
        </h2>

        <p>
            Created by
            <strong>Mohammed Elmi Issak</strong>
        </p>

        <p>
            Founder &amp; President,
            Elmi Guray Academy
        </p>

        <nav>
            <a href="#original-content">
                Original Content
            </a>

            <span> | </span>

            <a href="#html-requirements">
                HTML Requirements
            </a>

            <span> | </span>

            <a href="#lesson-structure">
                Lesson Structure
            </a>

            <span> | </span>

            <a href="#language-standard">
                Language Standard
            </a>
        </nav>

    </header>

    <hr>

    <main>

        <section id="original-content">

            <h2>
                Original EGA Content Policy
            </h2>

            <p>
                Every Elmi Guray Academy lesson must be an
                <strong>original EGA lesson</strong>.
            </p>

            <p>
                Lessons must not copy, closely rewrite, or closely imitate
                material from another instructor, course, book, website,
                video, or educational platform.
            </p>

            <p>
                Any transcript or lesson text supplied to EGA should only
                be used to identify the general topic that needs to be
                taught.
            </p>

            <p>
                The original wording, sentence structure, examples,
                activities, explanations, and lesson organization must not
                be copied.
            </p>

            <p>
                Every lesson must be newly written and presented as an
                official Elmi Guray Academy course created by:
            </p>

            <address>
                <strong>Mohammed Elmi Issak</strong><br>
                Founder &amp; President<br>
                Elmi Guray Academy
            </address>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                Information That Must Not Appear
            </h2>

            <ul>
                <li>
                    Do not mention another course platform.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Do not mention another instructor.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Do not present another instructor's introduction
                    as EGA content.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Do not copy another instructor's examples.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Do not retain another instructor's name.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Do not claim that copied material was created by EGA.
                </li>
            </ul>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section id="html-requirements">

            <h2>
                Complete HTML Document Requirement
            </h2>

            <p>
                Every lesson must be supplied as one complete,
                standalone HTML document.
            </p>

            <p>
                The document must begin with:
            </p>

            <pre><code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;</code></pre>

            <p>
                The document must include the complete HTML structure:
            </p>

            <pre><code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
&lt;html lang="en"&gt;

&lt;head&gt;
    &lt;meta charset="UTF-8"&gt;

    &lt;meta
        name="viewport"
        content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"
    &gt;

    &lt;title&gt;Lesson Title&lt;/title&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;

&lt;body&gt;

    Lesson content goes here.

&lt;/body&gt;

&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre>

            <p>
                Students must be able to save the lesson as an HTML file
                and open it directly in a browser.
            </p>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                GFFDO Requirement
            </h2>

            <p>
                EGA code updates must follow the
                <strong>GFFDO</strong> method.
            </p>

            <p>
                GFFDO means:
            </p>

            <blockquote>
                <strong>Give Full File, Delete Old.</strong>
            </blockquote>

            <p>
                When updating a lesson file:
            </p>

            <ol>
                <li>
                    Provide the complete replacement file.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Do not provide only small replacement lines.
                </li>

                <li>
                    The old file content should be deleted.
                </li>

                <li>
                    The complete new file should be pasted.
                </li>

                <li>
                    The file should then be saved and tested.
                </li>
            </ol>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                File Name Requirement
            </h2>

            <p>
                Every lesson must include a clear filename.
            </p>

            <p>
                Example:
            </p>

            <pre><code>lesson-01-ai-tools-course-introduction.html</code></pre>

            <p>
                File names should:
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>
                    Use lowercase letters.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Use hyphens between words.
                </li>

                <li>
                    End with <strong>.html</strong>.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Describe the lesson topic clearly.
                </li>
            </ul>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                HTML Learning Requirement
            </h2>

            <p>
                The lesson content must be written as a real HTML webpage.
            </p>

            <p>
                Students should learn two subjects at the same time:
            </p>

            <ol>
                <li>
                    The main lesson topic.
                </li>

                <li>
                    The HTML format used to present the lesson.
                </li>
            </ol>

            <p>
                For example, an AI lesson should teach the AI topic while
                also showing students how headings, paragraphs, links,
                images, lists, forms, and semantic elements work.
            </p>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                Required HTML Elements
            </h2>

            <p>
                Lessons should use appropriate HTML elements throughout
                the page.
            </p>

            <table border="1">

                <thead>

                    <tr>
                        <th>HTML Element</th>
                        <th>Purpose</th>
                    </tr>

                </thead>

                <tbody>

                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <code>&lt;header&gt;</code>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Contains the lesson introduction and title.
                        </td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <code>&lt;nav&gt;</code>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Contains navigation links.
                        </td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <code>&lt;main&gt;</code>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Contains the main lesson content.
                        </td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <code>&lt;section&gt;</code>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Groups related lesson content.
                        </td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <code>&lt;article&gt;</code>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Contains independent learning content when
                            appropriate.
                        </td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <code>&lt;footer&gt;</code>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Contains academy information and lesson
                            closing content.
                        </td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code> to
                            <code>&lt;h6&gt;</code>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Organize page titles and section headings.
                        </td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <code>&lt;p&gt;</code>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Creates paragraphs.
                        </td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <code>&lt;strong&gt;</code>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Marks important text.
                        </td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <code>&lt;em&gt;</code>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Adds emphasis to text.
                        </td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <code>&lt;a&gt;</code>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Creates a clickable link.
                        </td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <code>&lt;img&gt;</code>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Displays an image.
                        </td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <code>&lt;ul&gt;</code>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Creates an unordered list.
                        </td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <code>&lt;ol&gt;</code>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Creates an ordered list.
                        </td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <code>&lt;li&gt;</code>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Creates a list item.
                        </td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <code>&lt;table&gt;</code>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Presents information in rows and columns.
                        </td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <code>&lt;form&gt;</code>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Contains interactive form controls.
                        </td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <code>&lt;fieldset&gt;</code>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Groups related form questions.
                        </td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <code>&lt;legend&gt;</code>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Gives a title to a fieldset.
                        </td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <code>&lt;label&gt;</code>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Describes an input control.
                        </td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <code>&lt;input&gt;</code>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Collects user information or answers.
                        </td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <code>&lt;button&gt;</code>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Creates a clickable button.
                        </td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <code>&lt;pre&gt;</code>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Preserves code spacing and line breaks.
                        </td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <code>&lt;code&gt;</code>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Identifies programming code.
                        </td>
                    </tr>

                </tbody>

            </table>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                HTML Element Explanation Standard
            </h2>

            <p>
                Every newly introduced HTML element should be explained.
            </p>

            <p>
                The explanation should include:
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>
                    What the element does.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Its opening tag.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Its closing tag, when required.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Important attributes.
                </li>

                <li>
                    A practical example.
                </li>

                <li>
                    The expected browser output.
                </li>

                <li>
                    When the element should be used.
                </li>
            </ul>

            <h3>
                Example: Anchor Element
            </h3>

            <p>
                The <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> element creates a clickable
                link.
            </p>

            <pre><code>&lt;a href="https://example.com"&gt;
    Visit Example
&lt;/a&gt;</code></pre>

            <ul>
                <li>
                    <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> is the opening tag.
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Visit Example</strong> is the link text.
                </li>

                <li>
                    <code>&lt;/a&gt;</code> is the closing tag.
                </li>

                <li>
                    The <code>href</code> attribute contains the
                    destination.
                </li>
            </ul>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                Image Requirement
            </h2>

            <p>
                Lessons may include the official Elmi Guray Academy logo.
            </p>

            <pre><code>&lt;img
    src="ega-logo.png"
    alt="Elmi Guray Academy logo"
    width="180"
&gt;</code></pre>

            <p>
                The image explanation must identify:
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>
                    The <code>src</code> attribute.
                </li>

                <li>
                    The <code>alt</code> attribute.
                </li>

                <li>
                    The image filename.
                </li>

                <li>
                    The correct folder location.
                </li>

                <li>
                    The fact that <code>&lt;img&gt;</code> does not use
                    a closing tag.
                </li>
            </ul>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section id="lesson-structure">

            <h2>
                Required Lesson Structure
            </h2>

            <p>
                Every EGA lesson must contain the following major parts.
            </p>

            <ol>

                <li>
                    <strong>Technical Explanation — English</strong>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Technical Explanation — Somali</strong>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>
                        GAL — General Analogy Learning — English
                    </strong>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>GAL — Somali</strong>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Practical HTML Examples</strong>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Browser Output Examples</strong>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Important Rules</strong>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Common Beginner Mistakes</strong>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Multiple-Choice Practice Activity</strong>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Answer Key</strong>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Remember Summary</strong>
                </li>

            </ol>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                Technical Explanation — English
            </h2>

            <p>
                The English technical section must explain the lesson
                topic clearly and professionally.
            </p>

            <p>
                It should:
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>
                    Introduce the topic.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Explain important terms.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Use short and understandable paragraphs.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Include practical examples.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Explain the HTML used in the lesson.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Progress from simple ideas to more advanced ideas.
                </li>
            </ul>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                Farsamo — Somali
            </h2>

            <p>
                The Somali section must teach the same subject clearly
                for Somali-speaking students.
            </p>

            <p>
                The Somali explanation should not be a confusing
                word-for-word translation.
            </p>

            <p>
                It should use clear Somali explanations while preserving
                important technical terms such as:
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>HTML</li>
                <li>AI</li>
                <li>Developer</li>
                <li>Element</li>
                <li>Tag</li>
                <li>Attribute</li>
                <li>Browser</li>
                <li>Link</li>
                <li>Image</li>
                <li>Code</li>
            </ul>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                GAL — General Analogy Learning
            </h2>

            <p>
                Every lesson must include an everyday analogy that helps
                beginners understand the technical idea.
            </p>

            <p>
                The analogy should be included in:
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>English</li>
                <li>Somali</li>
            </ul>

            <p>
                Suitable analogy topics may include:
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>A school</li>
                <li>A house</li>
                <li>A road system</li>
                <li>A toolbox</li>
                <li>A library</li>
                <li>A restaurant</li>
                <li>A textbook</li>
                <li>A carpenter</li>
                <li>A teacher and student</li>
            </ul>

            <p>
                The analogy must directly connect to the lesson concept.
            </p>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                Practical HTML Examples
            </h2>

            <p>
                Code examples must appear inside
                <code>&lt;pre&gt;</code> and
                <code>&lt;code&gt;</code>.
            </p>

            <p>
                HTML characters must be escaped so that students can see
                the code instead of the browser interpreting it.
            </p>

            <pre><code>&amp;lt;h1&amp;gt;Elmi Guray Academy&amp;lt;/h1&amp;gt;</code></pre>

            <p>
                In the browser, the escaped code will appear as:
            </p>

            <pre><code>&lt;h1&gt;Elmi Guray Academy&lt;/h1&gt;</code></pre>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                Browser Output Examples
            </h2>

            <p>
                When useful, the lesson should show both:
            </p>

            <ol>
                <li>The HTML source code.</li>
                <li>The result produced by the browser.</li>
            </ol>

            <h3>
                HTML Code
            </h3>

            <pre><code>&lt;p&gt;
    Welcome to Elmi Guray Academy.
&lt;/p&gt;</code></pre>

            <h3>
                Browser Output
            </h3>

            <p>
                Welcome to Elmi Guray Academy.
            </p>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                Important Rules
            </h2>

            <p>
                Every lesson must include rules students should remember.
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>
                    Write valid HTML.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Use opening and closing tags correctly.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Save the file with the correct extension.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Use lowercase filenames.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Check image and link paths carefully.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Open the file in a browser and test it.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Read and understand code before copying it.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Never share passwords or secret keys.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Use AI to support learning, not to avoid learning.
                </li>
            </ul>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                Common Beginner Mistakes
            </h2>

            <ul>
                <li>
                    Forgetting a closing tag.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Misspelling an HTML tag.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Using the wrong image filename.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Using uppercase letters when the actual filename is
                    lowercase.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Saving the file as
                    <code>.txt</code> instead of
                    <code>.html</code>.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Placing code outside the
                    <code>&lt;body&gt;</code>.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Using heading tags only to make text large.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Copying AI-generated code without testing it.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Depending on AI without understanding the result.
                </li>
            </ul>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                Multiple-Choice Practice Activity
            </h2>

            <p>
                Practical activities should normally use multiple-choice
                questions.
            </p>

            <form>

                <fieldset>

                    <legend>
                        1. What does GFFDO mean?
                    </legend>

                    <label>
                        <input
                            type="radio"
                            name="question1"
                            value="a"
                        >
                        Give Fast File, Delete Output
                    </label>

                    <br>

                    <label>
                        <input
                            type="radio"
                            name="question1"
                            value="b"
                        >
                        Give Full File, Delete Old
                    </label>

                    <br>

                    <label>
                        <input
                            type="radio"
                            name="question1"
                            value="c"
                        >
                        Generate Final Folder, Download Online
                    </label>

                </fieldset>

                <br>

                <fieldset>

                    <legend>
                        2. Which element displays an image?
                    </legend>

                    <label>
                        <input
                            type="radio"
                            name="question2"
                            value="a"
                        >
                        &lt;a&gt;
                    </label>

                    <br>

                    <label>
                        <input
                            type="radio"
                            name="question2"
                            value="b"
                        >
                        &lt;p&gt;
                    </label>

                    <br>

                    <label>
                        <input
                            type="radio"
                            name="question2"
                            value="c"
                        >
                        &lt;img&gt;
                    </label>

                </fieldset>

                <br>

                <fieldset>

                    <legend>
                        3. Which element creates a link?
                    </legend>

                    <label>
                        <input
                            type="radio"
                            name="question3"
                            value="a"
                        >
                        &lt;a&gt;
                    </label>

                    <br>

                    <label>
                        <input
                            type="radio"
                            name="question3"
                            value="b"
                        >
                        &lt;img&gt;
                    </label>

                    <br>

                    <label>
                        <input
                            type="radio"
                            name="question3"
                            value="c"
                        >
                        &lt;table&gt;
                    </label>

                </fieldset>

                <br>

                <fieldset>

                    <legend>
                        4. How should transcripts from another course be
                        used?
                    </legend>

                    <label>
                        <input
                            type="radio"
                            name="question4"
                            value="a"
                        >
                        Copy the original wording
                    </label>

                    <br>

                    <label>
                        <input
                            type="radio"
                            name="question4"
                            value="b"
                        >
                        Use only the general topic and create an original
                        EGA lesson
                    </label>

                    <br>

                    <label>
                        <input
                            type="radio"
                            name="question4"
                            value="c"
                        >
                        Keep the original instructor's name
                    </label>

                </fieldset>

                <br>

                <button type="submit">
                    Submit Answers
                </button>

            </form>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                Answer Key
            </h2>

            <ol>
                <li>
                    B — Give Full File, Delete Old.
                </li>

                <li>
                    C — <code>&lt;img&gt;</code>.
                </li>

                <li>
                    A — <code>&lt;a&gt;</code>.
                </li>

                <li>
                    B — Use only the general topic and create an original
                    EGA lesson.
                </li>
            </ol>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section id="language-standard">

            <h2>
                Lesson Language Standard
            </h2>

            <p>
                Every lesson must be:
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>Professional</li>
                <li>Beginner-friendly</li>
                <li>Original</li>
                <li>Clear</li>
                <li>Progressive</li>
                <li>Suitable for self-study</li>
                <li>Suitable for classroom teaching</li>
                <li>Easy to open in a browser</li>
            </ul>

            <p>
                Sentences should be clear and not unnecessarily
                complicated.
            </p>

            <p>
                Technical vocabulary should be introduced gradually and
                explained before students are expected to use it.
            </p>

        </section>

        <hr>

        <section>

            <h2>
                Permanent EGA Lesson Identity
            </h2>

            <p>
                Every lesson should be presented as part of:
            </p>

            <article>

                <h3>
